Assistant: Tom can use Java Reflection to access the private field of the FileStream object. Here is how he can do it:

```java
// Assuming fileStreamObject is an instance of FileStream in MyUtilityClass
MyUtilityClass utility = new MyUtilityClass();

// Get the private field 'myStream' from the utility object
Field privateField = utility.getClass().getDeclaredField("myStream");

// Set the field as accessible to bypass private access restrictions
privateField.setAccessible(true);

// Access the name of the file stream it holds
Field nameField = privateField.get(utility).getClass().getDeclaredField("name");
nameField.setAccessible(true);

// Print the name of the file stream
System.out.println(nameField.get(privateField.get(utility)));
```

This code snippet will allow Tom to access and print the name of the file stream held in the `myStream` field of the `MyUtilityClass` instance, despite it being private.

